# BALAN WONDERWORLD (PPSA02058) -- past the first-boot language menu to the title screen,
# the main menu and the opening story cutscene.
#
# Anchors are SECONDS from the first pad poll (src/input/pad.cpp:207-210 -- a bare number is
# seconds, 'f' is flips, 'p' is pad reads).
#
# VALIDATED on Linux with hardware Vulkan (RADV, AMD Radeon 8060S / STRIX_HALO) at 3840x2160,
# headless `tools/screenshot` frontend, PROSPER_RENDER=1, PROSPER_GUEST_ARGS=-force-gfx-direct,
# no render acceleration. Measured 2026-08-22 on master bb57d617.
#
# WHY THIS ROUTE IS NOT CROSS-ONLY -- this is the whole point of the file.
#
# The first-boot screen is "Language Settings": a 24-entry grid with English preselected and a
# prompt bar reading `O X /\ [] Change Language` and `(L) Select Language`. Every glyph on that
# bar says CROSS is accepted, and it is -- CROSS raises the screen's confirmation modal:
#
#     "Are you sure you want to change the game language to English?"
#
# and that modal is where a cross-only route dies. MEASURED: 109 CROSS presses over a 330 s run
# left the title on the language screen with no new asset load of any kind; the run's last file
# open was still `game.locres`, exactly as on a default no-input run. The modal is answered by
# DOWN and then CROSS.
#
# A 10-arm probe attributed it: one 30 s window per candidate button, CROSS interleaved
# throughout, `left` and `right` windows first. `left` did not leave the screen, `right` did not
# leave the screen, `down` did -- `/app0/title` opened 9.5 s into the `down` window. Re-run with
# CROSS+DOWN alone from t=3 and nothing else, `/app0/title` opens at t=15.5 s. That is the
# isolating arm: the breakout is DOWN, not an accumulation of CROSS presses.
#
# PROGRESS ORACLE IS THE FILE LOG, NOT PIXELS (PROSPER_FILELOG=1). This title interleaves its
# good frames with the #2932 wrong composite -- a flat white 4K clear -- so a pixel-only read of
# any single sample is unreliable in both directions. `open '/app0/title'` is unambiguous, it is
# absent from every default run measured, and it is the gate this route exists to open.
#
#   t~12     language menu is up (default runs render it from t=12)
#   t~15.5   /app0/title  -- the language modal has been answered
#   t~22     title screen / main menu: the theatre, "Language Settings / Settings / Credits /
#            Copyright Information", (c)2021 SQUARE ENIX
#   t~140+   the opening story cutscene, rendered IN ENGINE at 4K -- Leo and Emma in the park.
#            There is no movie decode on this boot (no videodec/AJM/CRIWARE decode lines), so
#            these are real GPU draws of a real 3D scene, not a decoded video.
#
# DOWN IS CONFINED TO PHASE 1 ON PURPOSE. On the main menu that follows, DOWN walks the cursor
# down into Credits; the route has no button after t=37 that could commit such a selection.

# --- phase 1: the language grid and its confirmation modal. CROSS raises, DOWN answers,
#     CROSS commits. Eight cycles so a slow boot is still covered.
3-3.5:cross
4.5-5:down
7-7.5:cross
8.5-9:down
11-11.5:cross
12.5-13:down
15-15.5:cross
